  "Id": 1707,
  "Title": "Writing Courses for AKU Staff",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Eight week writing courses aimed at developing the English writing skills of staff",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClass23047307F81A414FB2D1B4DF661BEC76\">This year ELE_net developed Writing courses for AKU staff in response to survey feedback asking for support in developing their writing skills, The first eight-week B1 course was successfully delivered online in April. It was well received by course participants. They enjoyed working through the interactive course materials and receiving detailed feedback from their tutor on their writing submissions. <br><br>The aim of these courses is to help AKU staff write correctly, clearly and concisely so their writing can be clearly understood by the reader. Course topics include&#58; writing emails for an external audience; writing about figures and data; writing a project update; and report writing.<br><br>Writing clearly and correctly is an important part of many staff members\u2019 day-to-day work at AKU. These writing course will help increase your skills and boost your confidence so you can operate more effectively in your work at AKU</div><div class=\"ExternalClass23047307F81A414FB2D1B4DF661BEC76\"><div><br></div><div>\u201c\u201cIt was a great experience to attend this online course. Thank you so much for your valuable feedback and support.\u201d&#160; Komal Saleem, Senior Assistant.<br></div></div>",
